dren. The priority is for children to be able to access safe treatment, preferably in Australian hospitals. In Australia, the sponsor of the drug DFMO has applied to the TGA for its registration for the treatment of neuroblastoma. The TGA has begun a priority review of the application. The minister is examining all options for interim funding for DFMO while the TGA evaluation process is ongoing. Sue Lines Senators, may I remind you that all advisers in this place need to be seated at all times. Jordon Steele-John I seek leave to make a one-minute statement. Sue Lines Leave is granted. Jordon Steele-John The Greens will not be supporting this motion today, but we do support the principles behind this motion and believe that greater funding should be given to both children with neuroblastoma and c","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-9475","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2024-07-04/6"}
